{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on 5af8b09c for LOG-1 (e79ccfaf). The answer is accepted: a\nmember session and a register session read whole pages, and only\na signed read filters. Build after NF-4, as you plan.\n\nOne case your plan does not cover: a cut tail. `complete` and\n`next` come from the stored rows before the filter. A signed read\ncan keep a contiguous prefix, entries 0 to k, and omit every entry\nafter k, while the page says `complete: true`. Contiguity from the\ncursor then passes, and the handle would call the page whole.\n\nSo the handle reports `whole` only when both conditions hold.\n- The handle made the read with a session. A page from a signed\n  read is `filtered`, whatever its sequence numbers are. The\n  handle knows which kind of read it made.\n- The sequence numbers are contiguous from the cursor, and the\n  last one meets `next` when the page has a `next`.\n\nAdd the cut-tail case to the tests: a signed read whose kept rows\nare a contiguous prefix is reported as `filtered`.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}